 ## Overview
-Local Ambient Occlusion (LAO) is a local shading technique that estimates light contributions from neighboring voxels rather than the entire volume, creating softer shadows and avoiding the complete occlusion of volume parts [S1][S3, unofficial]. It stands between local and global shading, typically by branching rays into random directions within a hemisphere and averaging accumulated translucency [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike global lighting, LAO is view-independent and can be precomputed or updated incrementally [S1][S3, unofficial].
